    <summary>Browser automation and AI test authoring from the terminal, by TestMu AI (formerly LambdaTest).</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Kane CLI by TestMu AI (formerly LambdaTest) runs browser tests written in natural language. Describe what to check, and Kane CLI drives a real Chrome browser, reports a verdict with evidence, and can save the run as a reusable test.

## Features
- Run natural-language objectives in your local Chrome
- Generate and refine test cases from a description
- Save runs as tests and run them again in CI
- Works with AI coding agents through skills and MCP

## Requirements
- A TestMu AI account (`kane-cli login`); runs use credits
- Google Chrome (stable) for local browser runs

## Notes
This package installs the npm package `@testmuai/kane-cli` globally with Node.js.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/LambdaTest/kane-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
